# What the checks need: the tests, ruff, the pre-commit hook, and the tool that builds the
# lock files. CI installs only requirements-dev.txt, which is generated from this file.
# The versions are kept the same as in requirements.txt:
-c requirements.txt
pytest
ruff
pre-commit         # runs ruff and pytest before every commit
pip-tools          # pip-compile, which writes the .txt files from the .in files
# The parts of JARVIS the tests import (they never load Whisper, Kokoro or a model)
fastapi
python-multipart
ollama
cryptography
httpx2             # the test client (fastapi's TestClient) needs it
